## 1. Manhattan Core – “The Classic 5‑Day Loop”

| Stop | Highlights | Opening Hours | Ticket (Adult) | Notes |
|------|------------|---------------|----------------|-------|
| **Statue of Liberty & Ellis Island** | Iconic statue, museum, ferry | 8:30 am – 5:00 pm (ferry) | $25.50 (includes ferry & pedestal) | Book in advance; 1‑hour window. |
| **Battery Park** | Waterfront promenade, views of the harbor | 6 am – 11 pm | Free | Great for a quick stroll before the 9/11 Memorial. |
| **9/11 Memorial & Museum** | Reflective pools, museum exhibits | 10 am – 8 pm | $28 | Reserve tickets online; 2‑hour visit recommended. |
| **Wall Street & New York Stock Exchange** | Financial district, Charging Bull | 9 am – 5 pm | Free | Guided tours available for a fee. |
| **Brooklyn Bridge** | Walk across to Brooklyn | 24 hr | Free | Best early morning or late evening for light. |
| **Times Square** | Neon lights, Broadway theaters | 24 hr | Free | Avoid peak crowds (mid‑afternoon). |
| **Central Park** | Green oasis, Bethesda Terrace, Bow Bridge | 6 am – 1 am | Free | Rent a bike or take a guided tour. |
| **Empire State Building** | Observation deck | 8 am – 2 am | $44 | Skip‑the‑line tickets save 30 min. |
| **Top of the Rock (Rockefeller Center)** | City skyline, NBC Studio | 8 am – 11 pm | $38 | Same‑day tickets cheaper than online. |

**Suggested Itinerary (3–4 days)**  
- **Day 1:** Statue of Liberty → Battery Park → 9/11 Memorial → Wall Street → Brooklyn Bridge (walk to Brooklyn).  
- **Day 2:** Times Square → Central Park (bike or walk) → Empire State Building (evening).  
- **Day 3:** Top of the Rock → Museum of Modern Art (MoMA) → Broadway show (book in advance).  
- **Day 4 (optional):** Free day – explore neighborhoods (SoHo, Greenwich Village) or take a day trip to the Hudson Valley.

---

## 2. Brooklyn Highlights – “The Brooklyn Explorer”

| Stop | Highlights | Opening Hours | Ticket (Adult) | Notes |
|------|------------|---------------|----------------|-------|
| **Brooklyn Bridge Park** | Waterfront, promenade, playgrounds | 6 am – 11 pm | Free | Great for sunrise photos. |
| **DUMBO** | Cobblestone streets, iconic bridge view | 24 hr | Free | Visit the Brooklyn Bridge Park’s “DUMBO” café. |
| **Brooklyn Heights Promenade** | Panoramic skyline | 24 hr | Free | Best at sunset. |
| **Prospect Park** | Large green space, Prospect Lake | 6 am – 11 pm | Free | Rent a pedal boat or take a guided tour. |
| **Brooklyn Museum** | Art collections, Egyptian artifacts | 10 am – 5 pm | $16 | Free admission on Wednesdays. |
| **Brooklyn Botanic Garden** | Cherry blossoms, conservatory | 9 am – 5 pm | $15 | Combine with the museum for a “Museum Mile” day. |
| **Williamsburg** | Street art, indie shops, food trucks | 24 hr | Free | Nightlife hotspot; check for pop‑up markets. |

**Suggested Itinerary (2–3 days)**  
- **Day 1:** Brooklyn Bridge Park → DUMBO → Brooklyn Heights Promenade → Prospect Park.  
- **Day 2:** Brooklyn Museum → Brooklyn Botanic Garden → Williamsburg (evening).  
- **Day 3 (optional):** Day trip to Coney Island (beach, boardwalk, Luna Park).

---

## 3. Cultural & Museum Circuit – “The Art & History Trail”

| Stop | Highlights | Opening Hours | Ticket (Adult) | Notes |
|------|------------|---------------|----------------|-------|
| **The Metropolitan Museum of Art** | World‑class art, Egyptian wing | 10 am – 5:30 pm | $30 | Free admission on Fridays after 5 pm. |
| **American Museum of Natural History** | Dinosaurs, planetarium | 10 am – 5:45 pm | $28 | Free admission on Wednesdays. |
| **The Museum of Modern Art (MoMA)** | Contemporary art, Van Gogh | 10 am – 5:30 pm | $25 | Free admission on Fridays after 5 pm. |
| **The Guggenheim** | Architecture, modern art | 10 am – 5:45 pm | $25 | Free admission on Wednesdays. |
| **The Frick Collection** | European masterpieces | 10 am – 5 pm | $20 | Free admission on Wednesdays. |
| **The New York Public Library (Stephen A. Schwarzman Building)** | Iconic reading room | 10 am – 5 pm | Free | Guided tours available. |
| **The Whitney Museum of American Art** | 20th‑century American art | 10 am – 5 pm | $25 | Free admission on Wednesdays. |

**Suggested Itinerary (3–4 days)**  
- **Day 1:** The Met (morning) → Central Park (afternoon) → MoMA (evening).  
- **Day 2:** American Museum of Natural History (morning) → The Guggenheim (afternoon) → The Frick (evening).  
- **Day 3:** Whitney Museum → New York Public Library → stroll along 5th Avenue.  
- **Day 4 (optional):** Day trip to the Brooklyn Museum & Botanic Garden.

